    description: "Found by the 2026-11-24 docstring staleness audit (dev 7e204b35b): a reviewer flagged it and a default-REJECT verifier re-reproduced it on a fixture of its own (reports under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/staleness_audit_11242026/review and verify). Corpus impact not measured. group_records keys groups by the remaining fields only (tier_projection.py:93-95): group_records([{'reason':'r'},{'reason':'r','pass':'a'}],'pass','passes') returns [{'reason':'r','passes':['a']}], and two identical key-less records come back as one group. Latent: every current producer sets the varying key (limits.py:110-114, 160-168; all_analyzers.py:233/246/373). A third list added to _GROUPED_LIMITS would hit it. r35, v10."  # 6202
